; A `let` binding a primitive is not representable in the term/proof encoding,
; so this file must be reported as not supporting proofs.
;
; The binding is wrapped in `(fail …)`, which is what makes it a regression test:
; global removal used to leave the declaration of the shared table the binding
; writes to inside the `fail`, where a scan of only the top level never found it,
; so nothing recognized the write as a global binding at all.
(datatype Math (Num i64))

(fail (let $bad (/ 1 0)))

(Num 1)
(check (Num 1))
